  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between iloprost and Fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase 1, mediated through Nodal modulator 1. This connection is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate that iloprost acts as a target for several compounds—Nodal modulator 1, Crisaborole, and Piclamilast—each of which has a known target of Fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase 1. The high scores in all three paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction between iloprost and Nodal modulator 1 remains unclear. The shared target of these compounds implies that iloprost may exert its effects through a common pathway, possibly by modulating Nodal modulator 1, which in turn influences Fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase 1. This suggests that iloprost could be a potential activator or regulator of this enzyme, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
